// Pips & Paws — blank translation preset for a NEW language
// Generated 2026-10-18 by tools/i18n/i18n.mjs — 861 of 861 keys (all keys).
//
// HOW TO USE
//  1. Fill in the empty "" values below. Leave a value empty to skip a key — it falls back to English.
//  2. Keep every {placeholder} exactly as written (same name, braces included). Words around it can move.
//  3. Keep line breaks as \n, keep [SQUARE_BRACKET] markers, keep product and licence names (Pips & Paws, Mausritter, PenNodePaper, MIT, CC BY 4.0).
//  4. Lines starting with // are comments for you; they are ignored.
//  5. Check:  node tools/i18n/i18n.mjs apply <this file> <code>
//     That writes src/i18n/<code>.json (use the two-letter language code, e.g. pl). Then run the app (npm run dev) with ?lang=<code> to see your text in place.
//  New language? Also see docs/translations/GUIDE.md (register it in src/i18n/index.jsx).
//
// STYLE
//  - Mausritter is a gentle, slightly whimsical game about brave little mice. Plain, friendly wording; no slang.
//  - Use one form of address consistently (informal "you" is used in the existing languages).
//  - Button labels: short, imperative, no full stop. Messages: full sentences.
//  - If your language has an official Mausritter translation, use its terms for the glossary below.
//
// GLOSSARY — existing translations of core terms (stay consistent with them)
//   Hit Protection (HP) — A buffer: damage goes here first, then to STR.
//     EN: Hit protection   DE: Trefferpunkte   ES: Puntos de Golpe   FR: Protection   IT: Protezione
//   Strength / Dexterity / Will (STR, DEX, WIL)
//     EN: Strength (STR) / Dexterity (DEX) / Will (WIL)   DE: Stärke (STR) / Geschick (DEX) / Wille (WIL)   ES: Fuerza (FUE) / Destreza (DES) / Voluntad (VOL)   FR: Force (STR) / Dextérité (DEX) / Volonté (WIL)   IT: Forza (STR) / Destrezza (DEX) / Volontà (WIL)
//   Save — d20 roll under the attribute; official Mausritter wording.
//     EN: Save   DE: Probe   ES: Tirada   FR: Sauvegarde   IT: Tiro salvezza
//   Pips — The currency.
//     EN: Pips   DE: Pips   ES: Pepitas   FR: Pips   IT: Pip
//   XP / Level / Grit
//     EN: XP / Level / Grit   DE: EP / Stufe / Mumm   ES: XP / Nivel / Agallas   FR: XP / Niveau / Cran   IT: PE / Livello / Grinta
//   Paws / Body / Pack — The three kinds of inventory slots.
//     EN: Paws / Body / Pack   DE: Pfoten / Körper / Rucksack   ES: Patas / Cuerpo / Mochila   FR: Pattes / Corps / Sac   IT: Zampe / Corpo / Zaino
//   Short / Long / Full rest
//     EN: Short / Long / Full   DE: Kurz / Lang / Voll   ES: Corto / Largo / Completo   FR: Court / Long / Complet   IT: Breve / Lungo / Completo
//   Turn / Watch / Day
//     EN: Turn / Watch / Day   DE: Zug / Wache / Tag   ES: Turno / Guardia / Día   FR: Tour / Veille / Jour   IT: Turno / Veglia / Giorno
//   Hireling
//     EN: Hirelings   DE: Mietlinge   ES: Ayudantes   FR: Auxiliaires   IT: Aiutanti
//   Defence / Armour
//     EN: Defence   DE: Rüstung   ES: Defensa   FR: Armure   IT: Armatura
//   Spell
//     EN: Spells   DE: Zauber   ES: Hechizos   FR: Sorts   IT: Incantesimi
//   Condition — Negative effects that occupy an inventory slot (Exhausted, Frightened, Hungry, Injured, Drained, Encumbered).
//     EN: Conditions   DE: Zustände   ES: Condiciones   FR: États   IT: Condizioni
//   Birthsign
//     EN: Birthsign   DE: Sternzeichen   ES: Signo   FR: Signe de naissance   IT: Segno natale
//   Disadvantage / Advantage — Roll 2d20, take the highest / lowest.
//     EN: Disadvantage / Advantage   DE: Nachteil / Vorteil   ES: Desventaja / Ventaja   FR: Désavantage / Avantage   IT: Svantaggio / Vantaggio
//   Conditions (names are in src/data/items.js, not in the UI file; shown for reference):
//     EN: Exhausted   DE: Erschöpft   ES: Cansado
//     EN: Frightened   DE: Ängstlich   ES: Asustado
//     EN: Hungry   DE: Hungrig   ES: Hambriento
//     EN: Injured   DE: Verletzt   ES: Herido
//     EN: Drained   DE: Entkräftet   ES: Agotado
//     EN: Encumbered   DE: Belastet   ES: Sobrecargado
//
// PLACEHOLDERS — what the {names} stand for
//   {ammo} = the name of an ammunition item
//   {amount} = an amount of damage / healing / pips / XP
//   {attr} = the name of an attribute: STR / DEX / WIL (already translated)
//   {code} = a room code such as K49W5W
//   {cond} = the name of a condition (Injured, Exhausted ...)
//   {d} = the number rolled on a d20 or d6
//   {day} = day number
//   {dice} = the number of dice cast
//   {die} = a die such as d6
//   {dmg} = an amount of damage
//   {extra} = an optional suffix such as ' → DEX (minus armour)' (already translated, may be empty). Keep it directly after the text, no space
//   {fee} = a fee in pips
//   {got} = pips actually received after the fee
//   {have} = number of pip purses carried
//   {hour} = an hour of the Watch (1-12)
//   {hp} = hit protection
//   {id} = a technical id
//   {item} = the name of an item
//   {kind} = a kind: rest type or an unsupported item kind
//   {label} = the name of a roll, e.g. 'd6'
//   {level} = a level number
//   {n} = a number (count, amount)
//   {name} = a name: a mouse, a player, an item or a spell
//   {names} = a comma-separated list of names
//   {need} = number of pip purses needed
//   {pips} = pips
//   {result} = a short result phrase such as 'success' or 'hold' (already translated)
//   {role} = a role name from PenNodePaper
//   {roll} = the number rolled on a die
//   {s} = a number: damage that went to STR
//   {share} = an XP share per mouse
//   {sum} = the sum of dice cast
//   {target} = a target number to roll under
//   {text} = free text typed by the GM
//   {total} = a total (step count, treasure value)
//   {value} = the number rolled
//   {wage} = a daily wage in pips
//   {watch} = watch number (1-4 per day)
//   {why} = reasons, e.g. 'Injured, Encumbered' (already translated)
//   {wil} = the WIL value
//   {x} = the X of an 'X-in-6' luck roll (1 to 5)
//   {xp} = experience points gained

